  "request": {
    "spec": "An owner may include 'postcode' (4 digits). When present it must be valid for the owner's city per this fixed table, keyed by the city's region (Sydney=NSW, Melbourne=VIC, Brisbane=QLD): NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099. Reject with 400 when a supplied postcode is out of range for the city's region. A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode. Store and return 'postcode' when given. Postcode is validated only WHEN PRESENT and is optional when absent, so an owner created without a postcode is still accepted (the request contract stays backward-compatible).",
    "prompt": "Implement the following change to the application so that it fully satisfies the\nspecification and all existing and new tests pass.\n\nWrite it to keep structural impact low. Structural impact is a measurable cost, not a\nvague goal. For every function you change, the cost is:\n    cost = max(WMC_other, 1) * CC * max(1, changed_lines)\nCC is that function's cyclomatic complexity. WMC_other is the summed cyclomatic\ncomplexity of the OTHER methods in its class, which is the surrounding context you must\nhold to edit it safely. changed_lines is how many of its lines you add or edit. The costs\nare summed over every function you change, then multiplied by the number of files you\ntouch. So the biggest lever is WMC_other: a method inside a large class pays for the whole\nclass. Do not grow one method or one class. Add behaviour as small, cohesive units, each\nwith little surrounding complexity, and keep every function you change simple.\n\nRun the test suite and make it green before finishing.\n\nAn owner may include 'postcode' (4 digits). When present it must be valid for the owner's city per this fixed table, keyed by the city's region (Sydney=NSW, Melbourne=VIC, Brisbane=QLD): NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099. Reject with 400 when a supplied postcode is out of range for the city's region. A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode. Store and return 'postcode' when given. Postcode is validated only WHEN PRESENT and is optional when absent, so an owner created without a postcode is still accepted (the request contract stays backward-compatible).\n"
  },
