    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nOptional `postcode` (4 digits) on owners: validated against the city's region only when present, otherwise accepted; stored and returned.\n\n- **NSW/VIC/QLD ranges** enforced (Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099); unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit code.\n- **Malformed** postcodes (e.g. `\"12\"`) \u2192 400.\n- **Absent** postcode \u2192 still accepted (contract stays backward-compatible).\n\n## Files touched (5) and why each is minimal\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `postcode` to `OwnerFields` with `pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`. The generated DTO gets the field (auto-mapped by MapStruct on both `Owner`\u2194`OwnerDto` directions, so store+return come for free) and a `@Pattern` that rejects malformed input as 400 with no code.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 one field + a trivial getter/setter pair (each CC 1). No existing method changed.\n3. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 one `postcode VARCHAR(4)` column (the test profile runs `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must be declared).\n4. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended a `NULL` to the 10 positional seed inserts to keep column counts matching.\n5. **`OwnerFieldsValidator.java`** \u2014 the region-range rule lives in a **new small private method** `validatePostcode`; the existing `validate` method gains a single call line, so its own complexity and body are untouched. This class's surrounding complexity (`WMC_other`) is just the trivial `supports()`, so the new logic sits where it costs the least.\n\n## Structural-impact notes\n- No large or complex method was grown. The only edits to existing functions are one-line additions (the validator call) and new low-CC units (accessors, the postcode helper).\n- The region table is inlined as a small `switch` in the new helper \u2014 same shape already used in `OwnerMapper` for `locality` \u2014 avoiding a new shared class and keeping the file count from growing further.",
